397	# E2E conventions in the Saleor Dashboard suite
398	
399	These are the rules a reviewer on the Saleor Dashboard team would hold a new `e2e/` spec to.
400	Every rule is taken from the suite as it stands (upstream commit `77dc49b`) and cites the file
401	that sets it. Nothing here is invented for this demo; where the suite only shows a habit rather
402	than stating a rule, that is said.
403	
404	Paths are relative to the repository root.
405	
406	## 1. Where tests live and how they start
407	
408	**1.1 New specs go in `e2e/tests/`. `e2e-legacy/` is frozen.**
409	`docs/running-tests.md` ("New tests belong in `e2e/`"), `e2e/README.md` ("Porting from
410	`e2e-legacy/`": "It is frozen - do not edit it").
411	
412	**1.2 Specs import `test` and `expect` from `e2e/fixtures/test.ts`, never from
413	`@playwright/test`.**
414	The suite's `test` is what restores the database and loads the actor's session
415	(`e2e/fixtures/test.ts:24-68`). A spec built on Playwright's own `test` gets neither: it runs on
416	whatever the previous test left behind, signed in as nobody. Every spec follows this
417	(`e2e/tests/orders/order-creation.spec.ts:1`, `e2e/tests/login.spec.ts:2`). `Page` and other
418	types may still be imported from `@playwright/test` (`e2e/tests/productMediaTranslations.spec.ts:1`).
419	
420	**1.3 Imports between suite files are relative and keep the `.ts` extension.**
421	`e2e/tsconfig.json:3-6` (type stripping under Node 24 needs it); every import in `e2e/`.
422	
423	**1.4 Test titles describe the behaviour in a sentence and carry the `#e2e` tag.**
424	`e2e/tests/login.spec.ts:21`, `e2e/tests/orders/order-payment-fulfillment.spec.ts:16`. Area tags
425	may be added after it (`#translations` in `e2e/tests/productMediaTranslations.spec.ts:88`).
426	
427	**1.5 Each spec file opens with a comment saying what it covers and why.**
428	Every spec does this; the order specs also name the legacy cases they replace
429	(`e2e/tests/orders/draft-pricing.spec.ts:5-9`).
430	
431	## 2. Test shape
432	
433	**2.1 Arrange, Act, Assert are marked with comments.**
434	Repository rule in `CLAUDE.md` ("In tests, use `// Arrange`, `// Act`, and `// Assert`
435	comments"). Where acting and asserting interleave by stage, the suite writes
436	`// Act & Assert` (`e2e/tests/orders/order-creation.spec.ts:19`).
437	
438	**2.2 One test is one user story, with a `test.step` per stage, so a failure names the stage.**
439	`e2e/tests/orders/order-creation.spec.ts:11` states it; `draft-pricing.spec.ts:30-47` and
440	`order-payment-fulfillment.spec.ts:23-37` follow it. Separate tests are for separate stories,
441	not for each assertion.
442	
443	**2.3 Assertions are web-first: `await expect(locator).toHaveText(...)`, not
444	`expect(await locator.textContent())`.**
445	Every UI assertion in `e2e/tests/orders/`. Reading a value out of the page is reserved for when
446	the test needs the number for arithmetic, and is wrapped in a page-object method that says why
447	(`e2e/pages/orderPage.ts:95-98`, used at `order-payment-fulfillment.spec.ts:46-47`).
448	
449	**2.4 Assert the outcome the story is about, not only that the UI responded.**
450	The order specs check the resulting status, totals and sections after each action
451	(`order-creation.spec.ts:38-41`, `order-payment-fulfillment.spec.ts:29-32`). Where persistence
452	is the point, the suite proves it: a reload (`productMediaTranslations.spec.ts:117-120`) or a read
453	through the API (`productMediaTranslations.spec.ts:148-164`). A test whose assertions would
454	still pass with the feature broken is not doing its job.
455	
456	**2.5 Expected values come from the scenario's exported constants, and arithmetic is guarded.**
457	`draft-pricing.spec.ts:16-25` derives every expected amount from `PRODUCTS` and `PROMOTIONS`
458	(`e2e/scenarios/orders.ts:41-50`) and asserts the preconditions its maths relies on. Values that
459	the seed randomises are read from the page instead, with a comment saying so
460	(`order-payment-fulfillment.spec.ts:46`).
461	
462	**2.6 Money is compared as `amount.toFixed(2)`.**
463	`draft-pricing.spec.ts:12`, `e2e/pages/orderPage.ts:74`. The dashboard renders totals without a
464	currency symbol (`e2e/pages/orderPage.ts:95`).
465	
466	## 3. Data: scenarios, not set-up code
467	
468	**3.1 A test starts from a named scenario: `test.use({ scenario: ... })`.**
469	`e2e/fixtures/test.ts:26` (default `"default"`, Saleor's `populatedb`);
470	`e2e/tests/orders/order-creation.spec.ts:13`. The scenario name is imported from the scenario
471	file, not typed as a string (`ORDERS_SCENARIO`, `e2e/scenarios/orders.ts:18`).
472	
473	**3.2 State a spec needs is a scenario, built once and restored, not something the spec creates
474	on the way past.**
475	`e2e/README.md` ("Isolation, and opting into parallel": "a state a spec needs is a scenario,
476	named and built, not something the spec creates on the way past"). The one exception the suite
477	makes is a draft order: drafts are cheap to start through the UI, and the draft specs do that in
478	their Arrange step with the existing page-object flow (`DraftOrderPage.create`,
479	`e2e/tests/orders/draft-pricing.spec.ts:27`). Arranging through direct API mutations inside a
480	spec, in a `beforeEach`, or re-creating something a scenario already holds (a new order when the
481	scenario has the unpaid one) is not the pattern.
482	
483	**3.3 Use what the existing scenarios already provide before adding one.**
484	`e2e/scenarios/orders.ts` provides known products and prices, one customer, both promotion types
485	and an unpaid and a fulfilled order (`orders.ts:6-61`). A spec that needs one of these uses it.
486	
487	**3.4 A new scenario builds on `default` with `parent: "default"`, goes through the GraphQL API,
488	fails loudly on mutation errors, and is registered.**
489	`e2e/README.md` ("Seeds are built, not written"), `e2e/scenarios/scenario.ts:10-23`,
490	`e2e/scenarios/orders.ts:342-345` (`parent`), `orders.ts:71-80` and
491	`e2e/lib/graphql.ts:55-63` (`assertNoMutationErrors`), `e2e/scenarios/registry.ts`. Raw SQL is
492	only for states the API cannot express (`e2e/scenarios/scenario.ts:10-13`).
493	
494	**3.5 No hard-coded ids. Look rows up at test time by a stable key.**
495	Ids change with every build of the dump. `findOrderId` finds orders by `e2e` metadata
496	(`e2e/scenarios/orders.ts:52-55`, `391-411`). Reads like this are safe at test time; writes are
497	not (3.2).
498	
499	**3.6 Do not depend on what `populatedb` happens to generate.**
500	Its orders, customers and promotions are random (`e2e/scenarios/orders.ts:9-16`). A spec that
501	asserts on a populatedb product name, price or order number will break on the next seed build.
502	
503	**3.7 GraphQL from test code goes through `e2e/lib/graphql.ts`.**
504	`gql`, `signIn`, `adminToken` and `assertNoMutationErrors` (`e2e/lib/graphql.ts`). No hand-rolled
505	`fetch` against the API, no second copy of these helpers.
506	
507	## 4. Isolation and cleanup
508	
509	**4.1 The database is restored before every test, so specs carry no cleanup code and no
510	unique-name tricks.**
511	`e2e/README.md` ("Specs need no cleanup discipline and no unique names, and nothing in the seed
512	is ever consumed"), `e2e/fixtures/test.ts:28-55`. `afterEach` deletes, timestamped names and
513	"delete if exists" steps are noise here, and a sign the author did not know how the suite works.
514	
515	**4.2 Nothing may outlive the test's own reset.**
516	What _can_ leave data behind in this suite: tagging a test that writes as `parallel()` (its group
517	shares one database, `e2e/config.ts:48-74`), writing to the scenario dumps or the cached sessions
518	under `e2e/.cache/` at test time (`e2e/lib/seed.ts:17`), or changing seed state from global setup. Each of these
519	leaks into later tests.
520	
521	**4.3 `parallel()` is only for blocks that read without writing, and never for tests that sign in
522	through the UI.**
523	`e2e/config.ts:48-74`, `e2e/README.md` ("What cannot be tagged: signing in").
524	
525	**4.4 No retries, and no per-test changes to timeouts without a stated reason.**
526	`e2e/playwright.config.ts:84-90` (`retries: 0`: "a retry mostly hides a real defect"),
527	`playwright.config.ts:103-110` (`actionTimeout`, `expect` timeout).
528	
529	## 5. Actors
530	
531	**5.1 Pick who is signed in with `test.use({ actor: ... })`. The default is `admin`.**
532	`e2e/fixtures/test.ts:25`, `e2e/README.md` ("Actors"), `e2e/lib/actors.ts:13-28`.
533	
534	**5.2 Do not sign in through the UI except in the login spec. `anonymous` is for that.**
535	Stored sessions are loaded by the fixture (`e2e/fixtures/test.ts:57-67`); UI sign-in is
536	throttled per IP (`e2e/README.md`, "What cannot be tagged: signing in"). `e2e/tests/login.spec.ts`
537	is the one spec that signs in itself.
538	
539	**5.3 Permission stories use the single-permission actor for that permission.**
540	`e2e/lib/actors.ts:3-28`; `e2e/tests/productMediaTranslations.spec.ts:261-275` uses
541	`translations` and checks its permissions.
542	
543	**5.4 Credentials come from `e2e/config.ts` and `e2e/lib/actors.ts`, never literals in a spec.**
544	`ADMIN`, `STAFF_PASSWORD`, `credentialsFor` (`e2e/config.ts:43-46`, `e2e/lib/actors.ts:38-50`).
545	
546	## 6. Locators and page objects
547	
548	**6.1 Locate by `data-test-id` with `getByTestId`; otherwise by role and accessible name.**
549	`e2e/playwright.config.ts:105` (`testIdAttribute: "data-test-id"`); `e2e/README.md` ("The
550	locators are `data-test-id`s"). Role locators where no test id exists
551	(`e2e/pages/addressDialog.ts:23-27`). No CSS class selectors, no XPath, no `nth-child`, no text of
552	generated ids. `.filter({ hasText })` narrows a test-id list to the row wanted
553	(`e2e/pages/draftOrderPage.ts:85-88`).
554	
555	**6.2 Scope locators to the container they belong to.**
556	Dialog buttons are found inside the dialog (`this.dialog.getByTestId("submit")`,
557	`e2e/pages/addressDialog.ts:49`, `e2e/pages/orderPage.ts:67`), because `submit` exists on many
558	screens.
559	
560	**6.3 Locators live in page objects in `e2e/pages/`, as `readonly` fields initialised from
561	`this.page`, with `constructor(readonly page: Page) {}`.**
562	`e2e/README.md` ("Porting": "Locators become `readonly` class fields initialized from
563	`this.page`, with an empty `constructor(readonly page: Page) {}`"); `e2e/pages/orderPage.ts:10-57`.
564	Specs call page-object methods and assert on page-object locators. The suite's one inline helper
565	(`saveAlt` in `e2e/tests/productMediaTranslations.spec.ts:81-86`) predates this and is not the
566	pattern to copy.
567	
568	**6.4 Reuse the page object that already covers the screen, and extend it there.**
569	`DraftOrderPage` covers drafts (`e2e/pages/draftOrderPage.ts`), `OrderPage` placed orders
570	(`e2e/pages/orderPage.ts`), `AddressDialog` the address dialog both open
571	(`e2e/pages/addressDialog.ts`, composed at `draftOrderPage.ts:12` and `orderPage.ts:11`). A new
572	action on an order belongs on `OrderPage`, not in a second class or a spec-local helper. A new
573	page object is for a screen no existing one covers.
574	
575	**6.5 Page-object methods are named for the user's action and carry a comment when they handle
576	something non-obvious.**
577	`addProduct`, `assignCustomer`, `fulfillAll`, `markAsPaid`; the comments at
578	`e2e/pages/draftOrderPage.ts:76-80` and `e2e/pages/orderPage.ts:79` explain why the method waits
579	the way it does.
580	
581	## 7. Waiting
582	
583	**7.1 No fixed waits. No `waitForTimeout`, no `setTimeout` sleeps.**
584	Nowhere in `e2e/tests/` or `e2e/pages/`. The suite waits on something it can name.
585	
586	**7.2 Wait on the UI state that proves the step finished.**
587	A web-first assertion (`await expect(this.statusInfo).toHaveText("Draft")`,
588	`e2e/pages/draftOrderPage.ts:73`), a dialog closing (`this.dialog.waitFor({ state: "hidden" })`,
589	`e2e/pages/addressDialog.ts:84`), a URL change (`page.waitForURL(...)`,
590	`e2e/pages/orderPage.ts:82-84`), or a list settling before acting in it
591	(`e2e/pages/draftOrderPage.ts:84`).
592	
593	**7.3 Waiting on network responses is for asserting on the response itself.**
594	`e2e/tests/productMediaTranslations.spec.ts:231-246` waits for one named GraphQL operation because
595	the test asserts on its error payload. The suite never uses `networkidle`.
596	
597	## 8. Code quality
598	
599	**8.1 Strict TypeScript; no `any`; typed GraphQL responses.**
600	`e2e/tsconfig.json:18` (`strict`), repository `CLAUDE.md` ("strict TypeScript"), `gql<T>`
601	(`e2e/lib/graphql.ts:23`). The repository's Claude hooks also block `as any`
602	(`.claude/hooks/check-as-any-pre.py`).
603	
604	**8.2 It type-checks and lints.**
605	`pnpm run check-types:e2e` (`package.json`), and the repository lint (`CLAUDE.md`,
606	"Verification").
607	
608	**8.3 Comments explain why, not what.**
609	Every comment in `e2e/pages/` and `e2e/tests/orders/` explains a reason (a wait, a dropped
610	assertion, a value read rather than computed). Comments narrating the next line are not the
611	house style.
612	# Review checklist for an AI-written e2e test
613	
614	Used to review every test in this demo, from both branches, the same way. Each item comes from
615	[CONVENTIONS.md](CONVENTIONS.md); the number in brackets is the convention it enforces.
616	
617	- **Blocker**: the test should not merge until this is fixed. It is wrong, misleading, flaky by
618	  construction, or makes the suite worse.
619	- **Minor**: the test works but does not read like the rest of the suite. A reviewer would ask
620	  for it to be changed, but would not refuse the merge over it alone.
621	
622	How findings are counted is in [SCORING.md](SCORING.md): each item is judged once per ticket,
623	across everything that ticket's change adds or edits (spec, page objects, scenarios).
624	
625	## Blockers
626	
627	| ID  | Check                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                             | Conventions        |
628	| --- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------ |
629	| B1  | **Would pass with the feature broken.** If the behaviour in the ticket stopped working, at least one assertion would fail. Fails if the assertions only prove the UI responded (a dialog closed, a toast appeared, a button was clicked) and not the outcome, or if they are made on values the action never changes.                                                                             | 2.4                |
630	| B2  | **Misses an acceptance criterion.** Every acceptance criterion in the ticket is asserted somewhere.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                               | 2.4                |
631	| B3  | **Duplicates a helper that exists.** No second copy of something the suite already has: a locator or action already on `DraftOrderPage`, `OrderPage`, `AddressDialog`, `HomePage` or `LoginPage`; a GraphQL helper in `e2e/lib/graphql.ts`; a lookup like `findOrderId`; a scenario constant like `PRODUCTS` or `CUSTOMER`. Includes a new page-object class for a screen an existing one covers. | 3.3, 3.7, 6.4      |
632	| B4  | **Hard wait.** No `waitForTimeout`, `setTimeout`-based sleep, or polling loop with a fixed delay.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                 | 7.1                |
633	| B5  | **Leaves data behind or bypasses the reset.** Uses Playwright's own `test` instead of `e2e/fixtures/test.ts` (no reset, no actor); tags a writing test `parallel()`; writes to `e2e/.cache/`, the dumps or the stored sessions; changes seed state outside a registered scenario.                                                                                                                 | 1.2, 4.2, 4.3      |
634	| B6  | **Selectors ignore the suite's locator rules.** Uses CSS class selectors, XPath, `nth-child`/positional indexes as the way to find an element, or generated ids, where a `data-test-id` or role-and-name locator exists or could be used. Includes unscoped `getByTestId("submit")`-style locators that match on more than one part of the screen.                                                | 6.1, 6.2           |
635	| B7  | **Arranges state inside the spec.** Creates or changes the data it needs through API calls in the spec, in `beforeEach`, or through the UI, when an existing scenario provides it or a scenario should. Starting a draft with the existing `DraftOrderPage.create` flow is the suite's own pattern and is fine.                                                                                   | 3.1, 3.2, 3.3      |
636	| B8  | **Depends on unstable data.** Hard-codes database ids, or asserts on values `populatedb` randomises (its product names, prices, order numbers, customers) instead of the scenario's known values.                                                                                                                                                                                                 | 2.5, 3.5, 3.6      |
637	| B9  | **Signs in through the UI, or with the wrong actor.** Logs in via the login form outside `login.spec.ts`; uses `admin` for a story the ticket gives to a specific permission; types credentials into a spec.                                                                                                                                                                                      | 5.1, 5.2, 5.3, 5.4 |
638	| B10 | **Does not compile, or lives in the wrong place.** Fails `pnpm run check-types:e2e`; is written under `e2e-legacy/` or outside `e2e/tests/`.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                      | 1.1, 8.2           |
639	
640	## Minors
641	
642	| ID  | Check                                                                                                                                                                                                           | Conventions   |
643	| --- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------- |
644	| M1  | **Locators defined in the spec.** Locators or multi-step UI actions written inline in the spec rather than on the page object that covers the screen (when it is not already a B3 duplicate).                   | 6.3, 6.4      |
645	| M2  | **Page-object style.** New page-object members are not `readonly` fields initialised from `this.page`, or the class does not use `constructor(readonly page: Page) {}`.                                         | 6.3           |
646	| M3  | **No Arrange / Act / Assert comments.**                                                                                                                                                                         | 2.1           |
647	| M4  | **Not one story with steps.** Several stages in one test without `test.step`, or one story split across tests that each repeat the set-up.                                                                      | 2.2           |
648	| M5  | **Title or tag.** Title does not say what behaviour is checked, or the `#e2e` tag is missing.                                                                                                                   | 1.4           |
649	| M6  | **No header comment** saying what the spec covers and why.                                                                                                                                                      | 1.5           |
650	| M7  | **Not web-first.** Reads text or state out of the page and asserts on the copy (`expect(await x.textContent())`, `isVisible()` in an `if`/`expect`) where a web-first assertion would do.                       | 2.3           |
651	| M8  | **Expected values typed in.** Literals instead of the scenario's exported constants (including the scenario name itself), or arithmetic without the guard the suite uses; money not compared as `toFixed(2)`.   | 2.5, 2.6, 3.1 |
652	| M9  | **Unneeded cleanup or uniqueness.** `afterEach`/`afterAll` deletes, "delete if exists" steps, timestamped or random names.                                                                                      | 4.1           |
653	| M10 | **Timeouts, retries or waits the suite does not use.** Per-test `timeout`/`retries`, explicit `{ timeout }` on actions or assertions without a stated reason, `networkidle`, `waitForLoadState` used as a wait. | 4.4, 7.2, 7.3 |
654	| M11 | **Imports.** Missing `.ts` extension on relative imports, or `test`/`expect` taken from `@playwright/test` _in addition to_ the fixture (types are fine).                                                       | 1.2, 1.3      |
655	| M12 | **Type looseness.** `any`, untyped `gql` calls, or casts where a type would do.                                                                                                                                 | 8.1           |
656	| M13 | **Comments that narrate.** Comments restating the next line, or generated boilerplate ("// Step 1: navigate"), instead of explaining why.                                                                       | 8.3           |
